IRON WIDOW
Chapter 1: The Selection
By Xiran Jay Zhao

# This is a placeholder text file for demonstration purposes

In the heart of Huaxia, where ancient traditions met mecha technology, eighteen-year-old Wu Zetian prepared for the day that would change her life forever. Today was the Selection—the day when girls from across the province would be evaluated to become concubine-pilots.

Zetian knew what everyone said: becoming a concubine-pilot was a death sentence. The male pilots inevitably drained their female counterparts of qi—life energy—during battle, leaving behind empty shells. But Zetian wasn't planning to be another casualty. She had a mission: to avenge her sister, whose qi had been drained by a celebrated pilot named Yang Guang.

As she stood in line with the other candidates, Zetian's fingers traced the small jade pendant hidden in her sleeve—the only possession of her sister's that remained. The Selection officials moved down the line, scanning each girl with qi-measuring devices. When they reached Zetian, the device lit up brighter than it had for any other candidate.

"Interesting," said the head official, studying Zetian with new intensity. "You have unusually strong qi potential. You might actually survive more than one battle."

Zetian forced herself to look demure, hiding the fire that burned inside her. "Thank you, sir. I hope to serve Huaxia well."

The official marked something on his tablet. "Report to the Chrysalis Center tomorrow morning. You've been assigned to pilot Yang Guang."

It took all of Zetian's self-control not to let her expression change. This was exactly what she had hoped for—but also what she had feared. Yang Guang, her sister's killer, would now be her pilot. The man she had come to destroy would be linked to her through the most intimate neural connection possible.

As she left the Selection hall, Zetian looked up at the massive mecha suits that loomed over the city—Iron Demons, they called them. Inside one of those, her fate would be decided. Either she would become another forgotten girl whose qi was sacrificed for a man's glory, or she would become something unprecedented: a girl who survived, a girl who fought back.

A girl who might even become an Iron Widow.

